WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.140
Chris: There are many different reasons why conflicts
arise in the workplace and failure to deal with these

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:12.590
issues quickly and effectively can have a serious
impact on the wellbeing of those involved, the wider

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:15.320
team, and any projects that they are working on.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:21.069
Leah: Conflicts will happen and having people
who are able to identify and handle conflicts

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:26.070
fairly and sensibly will remove or minimise
the impact that conflicts may likely have.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:33.170
Conflict situations can be very different in cause or
effect and there is no one solution that fixes all.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:36.660
This is where conflict management skills come in to play.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:42.980
Those familiar with conflict management will look
at each situation and utilise a style that is likely

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.530
to be effective, so let’s have a look at them.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:50.789
There are five conflict styles that
can be utilised to resolve conflicts

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:52.629
Chris: Accommodating

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:56.919
This style is about putting the
needs of others before your own.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:01:02.360
This can be useful if there is one party that
has different feelings about an issue to others.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:07.720
For those who don’t feel strongly about
something, keeping the peace is more important.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:14.750
Adopting an accommodating style can be useful to
resolve small issues quickly and can create a sense of

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:21.300
openness within the team as people feel that voicing
their opinion will not automatically create conflict.

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:27.700
The downside of this method is that you can be
seen as weak and prepared to give in quite easily.

00:01:28.389 --> 00:01:32.250
This is a technique that would not be
appropriate for dealing with more serious

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.990
issues that are affecting the team.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:35.880
Leah: Avoiding

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:41.529
This approach can be useful but can
also cause more problems that it solves.

00:01:42.009 --> 00:01:45.999
It involves removing one or more of the
conflicted parties from the project.

00:01:46.559 --> 00:01:51.559
This can be useful as it gives the removed
party or parties time and space to reflect

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:54.300
on the issues and it may resolve itself.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:02:01.379
Alternatively, if used in the wrong situation
this may cause more conflict as it can cause

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:07.680
resentment with team members, and it may also have
a detrimental impact on the projects progress.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:09.229
Chris: Compromise

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:14.190
This style is all about getting those that
are in conflict to agree to concede some of

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:17.030
their issues so that a solution can be reached.

00:02:17.679 --> 00:02:24.479
This style can be useful if there are critical time factors,
or it is imperative that a solution is required immediately.

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:30.930
The downside is that none of those involved in
the conflict is entirely happy as they may feel

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:35.880
that they have conceded to much which may make
them less likely to compromise in the future.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:37.470
Leah: Competing

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:45.200
This is a strategy that is only effective if there is a
serious issue and can only be used by those in authority.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:51.310
This involves forcing the view or opinion onto others
without giving any opportunity for disagreement.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:56.799
This leads to a win-lose outcome and may
leave those who disagree feeling aggrieved.

00:02:57.559 --> 00:03:02.770
This is a style that should be used when there
is a conflict situation that is unnecessary or

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.600
having a seriously damaging effect on the team.

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:07.700
Chris: Collaboration

00:03:08.389 --> 00:03:13.930
This method can be the most useful style to use as
it brings those that have differing opinions together

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:20.220
to discuss the problem with an open mind encouraging
them to focus on resolving the conflict by finding

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.890
solutions that are agreeable to all involved.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:29.420
Personal emotions are left out of this as the only
purpose is to find out what is the best solution

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:32.520
for the team which leads to a ‘win-win’ outcome.

00:03:33.259 --> 00:03:38.390
A downside to this is that it can be very
time consuming, and deadlines may be at

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:41.080
risk while time is taken to find a solution.

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:48.849
Leah: In any conflict situation and no matter what style
is used there are several steps to take that will make

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:51.930
a significant contribution to reaching a resolution.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:57.170
The first step is to remain calm
and be prepared to actively listen.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:04.330
When someone else is talking others involved in the
conversation are already mentally preparing a response.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:11.220
Active listening involves focusing on what
is being said and the points being made

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.899
rather than thinking about your own response.

00:04:14.709 --> 00:04:19.489
Being attentive and listening to the other person
gives you the opportunity to understand their

00:04:19.539 --> 00:04:25.039
point of view and creates the opportunity to
compromise and collaborate to find a solution.

00:04:26.079 --> 00:04:30.799
Chris: Being positive and patient are two other
factors in successful conflict resolution.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:36.550
By slowing down your emotional response and
considering that others involved may have positive

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:42.650
intentions rather than negative ones, will make a
significant contribution to finding a resolution.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:49.109
Finding a solution may take time as you explore
all the options but gives confidence to others

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:54.870
to give opinions and discuss their concerns to
reach agreement on an acceptable way forward.

00:04:55.940 --> 00:05:01.909
Leah: Once a conflict has been resolved it is important
to maintain open communications between those involved.

00:05:02.599 --> 00:05:09.240
Having an environment where team members can talk
freely and constructively on issues or concerns will

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:16.310
reduce the potential for conflict situations and raise
morale and therefore in turn increase productivity.

